# FROZEN BYTE FIXTURES - do not let a checkout rewrite them.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (rev5 P0-1)
# --------------------------------
# `tests/fixtures/pr4a/` holds the frozen PR-4A eval artifacts (one JSON report
# and five `.jsonl` ledgers) that
# `tests/unit/eval/pr4a-cost-provenance-gate.test.ts` judges. The test
# re-measures each file's sha256 and FAILS on any mismatch, so the bytes on disk
# are part of the contract.
#
# The repository root `.gitattributes` declares `*.json text eol=lf` but says
# nothing about `*.jsonl`. On a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` (this
# workstation's setting) an undeclared text file is converted to CRLF in the
# worktree, which would change the sha256 of every ledger and turn all five gate
# cases red in a clean clone. Measured, not assumed: an undeclared `.jsonl`
# checked out under `core.autocrlf=true` becomes CRLF, while a `.jsonl` declared
# `text eol=lf` here keeps its LF bytes.
#
# This rule is deliberately NARROW (one directory, the two frozen extensions) and
# it only REINFORCES the repository policy - it does not renormalise anything
# else, and it does not mark these files `-text` (they are plain LF text, so
# `text eol=lf` is the honest declaration).
# Patterns in THIS file are relative to this directory (git's rule for a
# subdirectory .gitattributes), so they are written without the leading path.
# `*.json` restates the root rule for this directory only; `*.jsonl` is the one
# the root policy does not cover.
*.json   text eol=lf
*.jsonl  text eol=lf
